4003-2.5.JR.LIEN.DEFAULT.MOTION\nL4@P0: Attorney or Party Name, Address, Telephone & FAX\nL5@P0: Numbers, State Bar Number & Email Address\nL6@P0: Plaintiff(s) appearing without attorney\nL7@P0: Attorney for Plaintiff(s)\nL8@P0: FOR COURT USE ONLY\nL9@P0: UNITED STATES BANKRUPTCY COURT\nL10@P0: CENTRAL DISTRICT OF CALIFORNIA - DIVISION\nL11@P0: In re:\nL12@P0: Debtor(s).\nL13@P0: CASE NUMBER:\nL14@P0: CHAPTER 13\nL15@P0: ADVERSARY NUMBER:\nL16@P0: Plaintiff(s),\nL17@P0: vs.\nL18@P0: Defendant.\nL19@P0: PLAINTIFF’S (DEBTOR’S) MOTION\nL20@P0: FOR DEFAULT JUDGMENT\nL21@P0: RE COMPLAINT TO AVOID JUNIOR\nL22@P0: LIEN ON PRINCIPAL RESIDENCE\nL23@P0: [11 U.S.C. § 506(a),(d); FRBP 3012]\nL24@P0: DATE:\nL25@P0: TIME:\nL26@P0: COURTROOM:\nL27@P0: ADDRESS:\nL28@P0: NAME OF DEFENDANT CREDITOR HOLDING JUNIOR LIEN:\nL29@P0: \nL30@P0: 1. Name of Defendant against whom default judgment is sought: _________________________________________\nL31@P0: _____________________________________________________________________ (Defendant).\nL32@P0: 2. Plaintiff (Debtor) filed the complaint in the above-captioned proceeding on .\nL33@P0: 3. The summons and complaint were served on Defendant by personal service mail service\nL34@P0-1: on the following date .This form is mandatory. It has been approved for use by the United States Bankruptcy Court for the Central District of California.\nL35@P1: December 2017 Page 2 F 4003-2.5.JR.LIEN.DEFAULT.MOTION\nL36@P1: 4. A true and correct copy of the completed Return of Summons form is attached.\nL37@P1: 5. The time for filing an answer or other response expired on .\nL38@P1: 6. No answer or other response has been filed or served by Defendant.\nL39@P1: 7. The default of Defendant:\nL40@P1: a. has not yet been entered, but is hereby requested.\nL41@P1: b. was entered on .\nL42@P1: 8. A Status Conference:\nL43@P1: a. is scheduled for (specify date, time, and place) ________________________________________________\nL44@P1: ______________________________________________________________________________________\nL45@P1: b. was held on (specify date, time, and place) ___________________________________________________\nL46@P1: ______________________________________________________________________________________\nL47@P1: 9. DECLARATION OF NON-MILITARY STATUS (Servicemembers Civil Relief Act, 50 U.S.C. chapter 50 (§§ 3901-\nL48@P1: 4043)). The undersigned counsel declares under penalty of perjury, with respect to each Defendant against whom a\nL49@P1: default judgment is sought by this motion:\nL50@P1: a. Defendant is not currently in military service. The facts that support this statement are as follows (see the\nL51@P1: court’s website for information about how to verify non-military status):\nL52@P1: b. Defendant is currently in military service. The facts that support this statement are as follows (if this box is\nL53@P1: checked, the plaintiff must attach a supplement to this motion addressing the requirements in 50 U.S.C.\nL54@P1: § 3931(b)(2) to appoint an attorney for the Defendant before entering a judgment):\nL55@P1: c. I am unable to determine whether or not Defendant is in military service. The facts that support this statement\nL56@P1: are as follows (if this box is checked, the plaintiff must attach a supplement to this motion addressing the\nL57@P1: bond requirement in 50 U.S.C. § 3931(b)(3)):\nL58@P1: 10. Defaulting party is not an infant or incompetent party.\nL59@P1: 11. Property at Issue:\nL60@P1: Plaintiff moves to avoid the junior deed of trust, mortgage or other encumbrance (Junior Lien) encumbering the\nL61@P1: following real property (Property), which is principal residence of Plaintiff(s).\nL62@P1: Street Address: ___________________________________________________________________________\nL63@P1: Unit Number.: ______________\nL64@P1-2: City, State, Zip Code: _______________________________________________________________________This form is mandatory. It has been approved for use by the United States Bankruptcy Court for the Central District of California.\nL65@P2: December 2017 Page 3 F 4003-2.5.JR.LIEN.DEFAULT.MOTION\nL66@P2: Legal description or document recording number (including county of recording):\nL67@P2:  See attached page.\nL68@P2: 12. Grounds for Determining Unsecured Status and Avoidance of Junior Lien:\nL69@P2: a. As of , the Property is subject to the following liens in the amounts specified securing the debt\nL70@P2: against the Property, which Debtor seeks to have treated as indicated:\nL71@P2: i. in the amount of $\nL72@P2: ii. in the amount of $\nL73@P2: is is not to be avoided;\nL74@P2: iii. in the amount of $\nL75@P2: is is not to be avoided;\nL76@P2: See attached page for additional lien(s).\nL77@P2: b. As of , Property is worth no more than $ .\nL78@P2: c. As a result, Defendant’s claim related to the Junior Lien on the Property is wholly partially unsecured.\nL79@P2: 13. Evidence in Support of Motion:\nL80@P2: a. The amount of the 1st lien identified in paragraph 12(a)(i) is based on\nL81@P2: attached and identified as Exhibit .\nL82@P2: b. The amount of the 2nd lien identified in paragraph 12(a)(ii) is based on\nL83@P2: attached and identified as Exhibit .\nL84@P2: c. The amount of the 3rd lien identified in paragraph 12(a)(iii) is based on\nL85@P2: attached and identified as Exhibit .\nL86@P2: d. The relative priority of the liens encumbering the Property is established by evidence attached as\nL87@P2: Exhibit .\nL88@P2: e. The value of the Property from paragraph 3(b) is based on\nL89@P2: attached and identified as Exhibit .\nL90@P2: f. Plaintiff submits the attached Declaration.\nL91@P2-3: g. Other evidence (specify): ______________________________________________________________.This form is mandatory. It has been approved for use by the United States Bankruptcy Court for the Central District of California.\nL92@P3: December 2017 Page 4 F 4003-2.5.JR.LIEN.DEFAULT.MOTION\nL93@P3: 14. Plaintiff requests that this court issue an Order granting the following relief:\nL94@P3: a. That the Property is valued at no more than $ .\nL95@P3: That Defendant’s claim related to the Junior Lien shall be allowed as a non-priority general unsecured claim in the\nL96@P3: amount per the filed Proof of Claim.\nL97@P3: b. The avoidance of Defendant’s Junior Lien is contingent upon\nL98@P3: Debtor's completion of the Chapter 13 Plan, or\nL99@P3: Debtor's receipt of a Chapter 13 discharge.\nL100@P3: c. Defendant will retain its lien in the junior position for the full amount due under the corresponding note and lien in\nL101@P3: the event of either the dismissal of Debtor's Chapter 13 case, the conversion of Debtor's Chapter 13 case to any\nL102@P3: other chapter under the United States Bankruptcy Code, or if the Property is sold or refinanced prior to:\nL103@P3: Debtor's completion of the Chapter 13 Plan, or\nL104@P3: Debtor's receipt of a Chapter 13 discharge.\nL105@P3: d. In the event that the holder of the first position lien or any senior lien on the Property forecloses on its interest and\nL106@P3: extinguishes Defendant’s lien rights prior to: Debtor's completion of the Chapter 13 Plan, or Debtor's\nL107@P3: receipt of a Chapter 13 discharge, Defendant’s lien will attach to the proceeds greater than necessary to pay the\nL108@P3: senior lien, if any, from the foreclosure sale.\nL109@P3: e. See attached continuation page for additional provisions.\nL110@P3: Date: Respectfully submitted,\nL111@P3: Signature of Plaintiff or Attorney for Plaintiff\nL112@P3-4: Printed name of Plaintiff or Attorney for PlaintiffThis form is mandatory. It has been approved for use by the United States Bankruptcy Court for the Central District of California.\nL113@P4: December 2017 Page 5 F 4003-2.5.JR.LIEN.DEFAULT.MOTION\nL114@P4: PROOF OF SERVICE OF DOCUMENT\nL115@P4: I am over the age of 18 and not a party to this bankruptcy case or adversary proceeding. My business address is:\nL116@P4: A true and correct copy of the foregoing